  "_approach": "Niche-era four-bar build that never loses the floor (classic bassline drops keep the kick running): 4/4 kick throughout, a shaker enters in bar 2, tambourine in bar 3, the clap picks up 8th flams from bar 3, closed hats double up, and bar 4 adds a swung snare roll that crests at 127 on the last 16th. Ref: the organ-bassline build into the drop on Jamie Duggan / Niche-era mixes, DJ Q 'You Wot'. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
